/*!
    \page creator-how-to-configure-tools-on-devices.html
    \previouspage creator-how-tos.html

    \ingroup creator-how-to-remote-linux
    \ingroup creator-how-to-build
    \ingroup creator-how-to-docker

    \title Configure development tools

    Configure development tools for devices in \preferences > \uicontrol Devices.
    The available tools vary depending on the device type and enabled plugins.

    \image {qtcreator-preferences-devices-desktop-tools.webp} {Tool configuration options for a desktop device}
    \caption Tool configuration options for a desktop device in the Devices
    tab in Devices preferences.

    To configure tools for a device:

    \list 1

        \li Go to \preferences > \uicontrol Devices > \uicontrol Devices.

        \li Select an existing device from \uicontrol Device.

        \li In \uicontrol {Type Specific} > \uicontrol {Run Tools on This Device}
            or \uicontrol {Source and Build Tools on This Device}, specify the paths
            to the tools.

            Or, in \uicontrol {Auto-Detection}, configure the auto-detection options
            and then select \uicontrol {Run Auto-Detection Now}.

        \li For remote Linux, Docker, and WSL devices, select
            \uicontrol {Kit Creation} > \uicontrol {Create kits targeting} to
            create a kit for using the automatically detected development tools.
            Or, select \uicontrol {Create Kits Now} to create kits for the
            toolchains that are already set up for the device.

            Kits for toolchains that target the operating system of the device
            use the device that you select in the list as run device. By
            default, this is the device itself. To have the kits use another
            device with the same operating system, for example a board that
            you cross-compile for on the device, select that device before
            creating the kits. The choice does not change kits that already
            exist.

    \endlist

    \sa {Use \QC variables}, {Build and Run}{How To: Build and Run},
    {Docker}{How To: Develop for Docker},
    {Remote Linux}{How To: Develop for remote Linux}, {Managing kits}
*/
